  "physical_environment": {
    "simultaneous_space_km2_per_1000_trainees": 0.12,
    "home_garrison_capacity_fraction": 0.1,
    "home_garrison_minimum_capacity": 2000,
    "rules": [
      "Training has exactly two physical contexts: permanent home/garrison infrastructure and field training.",
      "Every established city, capital, fort, fortress, fortified settlement, pass, military compound, military district, depot, or academy provides ordinary home/garrison training infrastructure without a separate construction tier.",
      "Field training requires suitable physical space but no prepared-field object, setup project, material cost, maintenance state, or quality tier.",
      "Specialist artillery, engineering, medical, household, estate, and similar drills still require their registered physical facilities; instructors and equipment remain separate determinants of training quality.",
      "Operational experience from march, siege, pursuit, command under pressure, and battle is separate from deliberate training and is awarded only to actual participants."
    ]
